\begin{ex}
Let $S \subseteq \Int^2$ be the successor relation on~$\Int$, i.e.,
$S = \Setabs{\tuple{x, y} \in \Int^2}{x + 1 = y}$, so that $Sxy$ iff $x + 1 = y$.

The \emph{reflexive transitive closure} of $R$ is $R^* = R^+ \cup
\Id{A}$.
\end{defn}

target:
