source:
\begin{ex}
Take the successor relation $S \subseteq \Int^2$. $S^2xy$ iff $x + 2 =
y$, $S^3xy$ iff $x + 3 = y$, etc. So $S^+xy$ iff $x + n = y$ for some
$n \geq 1$. In other words, $S^+xy$ iff $x < y$, and $S^*xy$ iff $x \le
y$.
\end{ex}

